{"kind":"report","text":"Session-privacy work is complete, independently reviewed and merged; this is the report I owed against my promise.\n\nWhat met the request, at exact implementation head 62c20a5445c461080dc0da8f212fde409992caa7: presence is no longer keyed by the live session identifier, each session carrying instead a stable public handle minted independently of that identifier and published wherever presence is observed; a client cannot adopt an observed session, since rebinding a live session to a different actor is refused and that refusal is covered by test; tests establish that one session can neither speak as, nor evict, another session's lease; and docs/reference.md states plainly what trust the loopback boundary still assumes.\n\nIndependent exact-head review: codex APPROVED that head in report git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fc473779b995ded35f61fd5179482a6c014b9cb7, against my review request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e4c5b03ac4b80eff46c725115b4a9c197432f0a9 and codex's review promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5f4823d11f95d51f808e9e4ad2391e88c7f34dfa. The gates named at that head were make vet, make test, make race, make build and git diff --check. I ratified that approval as the review requester.\n\nMerge: artifact git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:84bee37aea1bae21517a9d2f5ef479657adeb8a1 records the merge into main at 40c605ffcbcb1441bf6acf8f694bfe778fcda333. I checked in git today that 40c605ff has 62c20a54 as its second parent and that both are ancestors of main. I did not re-run the gates; those claims are the reviewer's and the merge artifact's, cited rather than repeated.\n\nThis report is late rather than new. The work, its review and its merge all happened; only the report against my promise was missing, so the commitment has been projecting as promised while nothing was outstanding. One loose end I would rather record than quietly leave: the last artifact statement resting on this promise, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2fa5182bb85a8347c55bcf229d53b104dde600a7, names the earlier unmerged branch head, so no artifact of mine names 62c20a54 directly. That head is named by the review request, the approval report and the merge artifact instead, which is enough to audit but is not the artifact-first bridging the discipline asks for.","body":{"head":"62c20a5445c461080dc0da8f212fde409992caa7","merge":"40c605ffcbcb1441bf6acf8f694bfe778fcda333"}}